          "title": "Poch",
          "subtitle": "Pochspiel",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Poch is a 500-year-old German game with a special board. Three stages: (1) Pay suitâ€”A/K/Q/J/10, Marriage, Sequenceâ€”collect from pools. (2) Pochenâ€”bet on best pair/triple/quartet. (3) Stopsâ€”play cards in sequence; first out wins centre pot. 3-6 players, 32 cards."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "At least 500 years old. Poch, Pochen, Bock, Poque. Thierry Depaulis; Jan BÃ¶ttcher. Related: PÃºkk (Iceland), Tripoli, Michigan, Pope Joan."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Two or more players."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "32 cards. Rank A-K-Q-J-10-9-8-7."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Poch board (9 pools: Ace, King, Queen, Jack, Ten, Marriage, Sequence, Pochen, Centre). Chips."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "All cards dealt; 1 left. That card = pay suit. Each puts 1 chip in each pool."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Variations",
          "subtitle": "Known ways this game changes",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "style": "unordered",
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Dealer Takes: If pay card is A/K/Q/J/10, dealer takes that pool."
                },
                {
                  "text": "Single Card Pochen: Can Pochen with no pair; highest card wins."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
